 "normalization": "neutral-forming set: dyes normalized to form a visual neutral density of 1.0 for a 5000 K viewing illuminant (dye peaks 0.93-0.95, NOT unit-peak). Note: the 100D datasheet's caption claiming its dye curves are 'peak-normalized' is factually wrong \u2014 its traced peaks are 0.92-0.94 and match E100's neutral-normalized curves.",
 "units": "diffuse spectral density (as published)",
 "source": "Kodak Alaris publication E-4000 (rev 8-18), Spectral-Dye-Density Curves, p.4 \u2014 extracted from embedded vector paths with cubic beziers evaluated on-curve (control points NOT used as curve points). Axis calibration from gridlines at 400/500/600/700 nm (70.64/137.46/204.28/271.10 pt, uniform to <0.01 pt) and 0.0-1.4 D (21.632 pt per 0.2 D).",
