  "conclusion": "identical dye set within digitization noise (2026-07-16 analysis); E100 vector chosen as canonical because the 100D chart is raster",
  "internal_consistency": "sum of extracted C+M+Y reproduces the chart's own published neutral/midscale curve to RMSE 0.013 D, max 0.015 D \u2014 confirms no curve mix-up and neutral-forming normalization"
 },
 "important_note": "Measured support 400.8-700.8 nm for cyan/magenta/neutral; yellow is drawn only to 680.8 nm (value ~0.008 D there) \u2014 entries beyond each dye's support are null; do NOT extrapolate or zero-fill in the data file (the engine's resample() treats beyond-support as 0 at build time, which is the documented bounded systematic). Cyan is still ~0.75 D at the 700 nm plot edge \u2014 a substantially larger long-wavelength truncation than Velvia 100 (0.29 D at 710); quantify before any narrowband build (see systematics register pattern).",
 "uncertainty": "vector geometry is exact to the printed plot; residual uncertainty is the datasheet plot itself (line width ~0.008 D equivalent). Cross-validation RMSE vs the independent 100D raster (0.006-0.011 D) bounds total digitization error.",
